dict(pas="2.6", w="孟武伯/Meng Wubo — Meng Yizi's son//Meng (a clan)//Wu (his posthumous name)//eldest son | 問/asked about | 孝。/filial devotion | ^子/the Master | 曰：「/said | 父母/father and mother | ^唯/only | 其/his — the child's | 疾/illness | 之/(marks the fronted object) | 憂。」/(they) worry over",
  l="Meng Wubo asked about filial devotion.\nThe Master said: “Father and mother —\nonly over his illness do they worry.”",
  i="Meng Wubo asked about being a good son. The Master said: “Your father and mother have one worry above all: that you may fall ill.”",
  n="孟武伯 is Zhongsun Zhi 仲孫彘, son of the Meng Yizi of 2.5. 唯…之… is a pattern to learn: the object is fronted and marked by 之, with 唯 'only' in front — 唯其疾之憂 'only his illness, (that) they worry over'. Zhu Xi reads it this way: parents' love is so complete that they fear only that their child may fall ill, and a son who takes that to heart will look after himself and keep out of trouble. He records an older reading too: a son should give his parents nothing to worry over except illness, which no one can help — never his wrongdoing."),
# ---------------- 2.7 ----------------
dict(pas="2.7", w="子游/Ziyou — the disciple Yan Yan | 問/asked about | 孝。/filial devotion | ^子/the Master | 曰：「/said | 今/nowadays | 之/'s | 孝/filial | 者，/(those who are) — 'the filial of today' | ^是/this | 謂/(is) called | 能/being able | 養。=yǎng/to feed, to support | ^至於/as for, coming to//to reach//to | 犬/dogs | 馬，/horses | ^皆/all | 能/can | 有/have | 養；=yǎng/feeding, support | ^不/not | 敬，/reverent | ^何/what | 以/by which | 别/to distinguish | 乎？」/(question)",
  l="Ziyou asked about filial devotion.\nThe Master said: “Today's filial ones —\nthis means being able to feed (parents).\nComing to dogs and horses,\nall can be fed;\nnot reverent,\nby what is it distinguished?”",
  i="Ziyou asked about being a good son. The Master said: “What passes for a good son these days means one who can keep his parents fed. But dogs and horses are all kept fed too. Without reverence, what is there to tell the two apart?”",
  n="子游 Ziyou is Yan Yan 言偃, a disciple known for his learning in the rites. 今之孝者 'the filial of today': 者 makes 孝 a noun, 'those who count as filial'. 養 is to feed and provide for (Zhu Xi: 飲食供奉); he marks it 去聲, the old reading yàng for supporting one's elders, which modern practice does not keep: we give yǎng. The 'dogs and horses' line can be read two ways. Zhu Xi: people feed their dogs and horses too, so if your care for your parents lacks reverence, how is it different from keeping animals? An older reading has dogs and horses as the ones who serve and support men. 何以别乎 'by what distinguish?' — 以 'by' with its object fronted as 何 'what'. 别 is printed in this form in the edition; it is the word 別 bié."),
