dict(pas="2.9", w="子/the Master | 曰：「/said | ^吾/I | 與=yǔ/with | 回/Hui — Yan Hui | 言/talk | 終/the whole | 日，/day | ^不/(he) not | 違，/differs, objects | 如/like, as if | 愚。/stupid, slow | ^退/(he) withdraws | 而/and | 省=xǐng/I examine | 其/his | 私，/private (life), (when he is) alone | ^亦/(he) also | 足/is quite enough | 以/to | 發。/bring out, illuminate (what was said) | ^回/Hui | 也/(pause after a name) | 不/not | 愚。」/stupid",
  l="The Master said: “I talk with Hui the whole day:\nhe does not object — as if slow.\nHe withdraws, and I look into his private life:\nit, too, is quite enough to bring (it) out.\nHui is not slow.”",
  i="The Master said: “I can talk with Hui all day long and he never raises an objection, as though he were dull. But when he has gone and I look at how he lives on his own, I find he brings to light all that I said. Hui is anything but dull.”",
  n="回 Hui is Yan Hui 顏回 (courtesy name Ziyuan 子淵), the disciple Confucius loved most, who died young. As with Ci in 1.15, the Master calls him by his personal name. 不違 here is not 'not disobey' but 'not differ': he takes in everything and asks nothing (Zhu Xi: 有聽受而無問難). 私 is his private life — Zhu Xi: when he is at leisure on his own, not when he comes to ask. 發 is to bring out into the open: what he does lights up the Master's teaching. The ending 回也不愚 turns the 如愚 'as if slow' of the first half inside out."),
